margin-left:18.0pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:justify&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: &amp;quot;PT Sans&amp;quot;, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;The proposed first floor rear extension, in conjunction with the
existing unauthorised ground floor rear extension, by virtue of its significant
mass and depth, would result in an unacceptable loss of daylight/sunlight and
create an undue sense of enclosure to the rear of the Nos. 22 and 26 Flambard
Road. The proposal is therefore contrary &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: &amp;quot;PT Sans&amp;quot;, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;to the National Planning Policy Framework (2024), Policy D3 of the
London Plan (2021), policy DM1 of the Harrow Development Management Policies
Local Plan (2013) and the adopted Supplementary Planning Document: Residential
Design Guide (2010).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:&amp;quot;PT Sans&amp;quot;,sans-serif;
